#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203683 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203900 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d05194c-249d-54fb-91f1-f614c0f5e584" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Non-Standard Relation"}] :question/id #uuid "7d7f9634-b8b1-5fb8-8f2a-9ecf32699231" :question/math-academy-id "e-14594" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{\\mathbb{Z}, \\mathbb{Q}, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n$X\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad \\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbb{Z} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{Q}$\n2. $\\mathbb{R} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{R}$\n3. $\\mathbb{Q} \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!}\\: \\mathbb{R}$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$R\\subseteq A^2$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{Z} \\cap \\mathbb{Q}$, which is false.\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{R} \\cap \\mathbb{R}$, which is true.\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\not\\subseteq \\mathbb{Q} \\cap \\mathbb{R}$, which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3fdfc79-dbfa-5820-82fb-402014341a3d" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Relations Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "55d5130d-ed4a-51ea-aa98-93232ef14f35" :question/math-academy-id "e-14624" :question/problem "Let $A = \\mathbb{R}$, and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie above the upward-opening parabola whose focus is at $\\left(0,\\dfrac14\\right)$ and whose vertex is at $O$. Express $R$ using set-builder notation." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A$, we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a \\: R \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\in R$\n- $a \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R} = \\mathbb{R}^2\n$$\n\nsuch that $y \\gt x^2$.\n\n![](images/26/26671c4dc03b13afc43172e486602bf3d647f8be911769c24a9e0523f591b64b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 \\:: \\: y \\gt x^2 \\Big\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203695 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff71f3f5-8383-5815-ba42-289f14e16b57" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Standard Relation"}] :question/id #uuid "1488c9fd-0fbf-57b6-bed5-3d060cf87a00" :question/math-academy-id "e-14634" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{\\mathbb{R}_0^+, \\mathbb{R}_0^-, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n$X\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad X\\supset Y$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbb{R} \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^-$\n2. $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^+$\n3. $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\mathbb{R}$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$R\\subseteq A^2$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $X\\supset Y$. For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\supset$ are interchangeable, and\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\supset$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R} \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^-$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\subset \\mathbb{R}$, which is true.\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^+$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^-$, which is false.\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ with the symbol $\\not\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\not\\supset \\mathbb{R}$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R} \\not\\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^+$, which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3fdfc79-dbfa-5820-82fb-402014341a3d" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Relations Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca67f47e-fe34-5071-8128-a4d0c970a725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200123} {:answer/id #uuid "320b3116-2015-5f3d-bb12-baca208ac7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z \\mid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200124} {:answer/id #uuid "53e17c87-fbc0-5a27-adab-02d008fbfe9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R \\mid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200125} {:answer/id #uuid "76244479-5982-5d04-9c4c-9f472afd1bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/re